Add Solaris inline IPS as a userspace Ethernet bridge using libdlpi, without
kernel changes. Enabled with --dlpi, the runmode validates reciprocal
interface/copy-iface pairs and starts one worker per input link. These links
must be dedicated bridge ports without IP addresses or another forwarding path.

ReceiveDLPILoop reads complete Ethernet frames using DLPI_RAW. Physical and
SAP promiscuity capture all destinations and EtherTypes; DL_PROMISC_NOLOOP
prevents recapturing transmitted frames. DLPIProcessPacket passes each frame
through DecodeDLPI and the normal FlowWorker stream and detection processing.

Suricata then invokes the packet's ReleasePacket callback, DLPIReleasePacket:
ACTION_DROP suppresses forwarding; otherwise dlpi_send sends the Ethernet
frame to copy-iface. The reciprocal worker handles the opposite direction.
As in AF_PACKET, bounded receive batches check shutdown and link/read errors
trigger a delayed reopen of the affected worker's DLPI handles.

